  "notes": "XPENG launched in Australia in late 2024 via distributor TrueEV. Factory-backed XPeng ANZ (XPeng Australia and New Zealand) took over distribution in April 2026; TrueEV and XPeng are in Federal Court proceedings. XPeng ANZ is currently selling: (1) the updated G6 (referred to as 'New G6' or 2027 MY in some press, arriving in AU showrooms July 2026) in four variants; and (2) the X9 electric people mover (available to order July 2026, deliveries commencing shortly after). While the X9 is sold as an EREV in China, Australia receives BEV-only versions — no EREV exclusion required for X9. The L03 BEV and G9L BEV are confirmed for AU launch in Q4 2026 (October–December) but not yet orderable as of September 2026; they are included as 'announced'. The L03 also has an EREV version; only BEV is listed here. The G9L will offer both EV and EREV in AU; only BEV listed. The L05 is scheduled for January 2027 and is not included. Note: the xpeng.com.au/g6-specification page as indexed appears to show the outgoing 2024 G6 (190 kW, 66 kWh, 435 km WLTP); the current 'New G6' specs are sourced from the store.xpeng.com/au configurator. Towing capacity for G6 and X9 is not confirmed in AU specifications reviewed. G6 segment is 'suv-small' per GoAuto press categorisation ('Small SUV over $45K segment').",
